  "title": "The Nota Simple line buyers never read",
  "source_article": "nota-simple.txt, land-registry.txt, buying-10-steps.txt, hoa-rules.txt",
  "post_text": "The figure that can catch you is the Catastro's valor de referencia. Since 2022, purchase tax is charged on that or on the price, whichever is higher, so look it up before you budget. It is not on the Nota Simple, and it is not the same number as the valor catastral on your IBI bill.\n\nThat said, order the Nota Simple anyway, and read all of it. It is the Land Registry's summary of who owns the property and what is attached to it. Mortgages, charges, easements, boundary descriptions and any court entries sit there in plain sight.\n\nIn Spain debts travel with the home, not the seller. Buy a property with unpaid charges, community fees included, and they become yours.\n\nYou will need the property's registry identifier, the IDUFIR. Around 10 euros online, arriving as fast as the same day, or under 4 euros in person at the registry.\n\nIt is also the document that proves the seller is the owner. There have been cases of squatters selling homes that were never theirs.\n\nTwo lookups, both cheap, both before you sign anything. The Nota Simple for what is attached to the property, the Catastro for what the tax will be charged on.\n\nOwning or planning to buy property in Spain? Bueno is trusted by homeowners from 25+ countries. getbueno.com",
