  "title": "The 700,000 euro wealth tax line",
  "source_article": "late-tax-penalties.txt",
  "source_slug": "wealth_tax_en",
  "post_text": "Below 700,000 euros of Spanish assets, a non-resident owes no wealth tax. That is the line, and it is per person, so a couple holding jointly each get their own.\n\nAbove it, the tax bites only on the value over the line, at progressive rates from 0.2 percent up to 3.5 percent on the largest holdings. There is no 2.5 percent top rate, whatever you have read.\n\nSome regions discount the tax heavily, but a non-resident is taxed under state rules by default. EU and EEA owners can opt into the rules of the region where most of their assets sit. Everyone else cannot. That is a choice you make on the return, not something that follows from where the property happens to be.\n\nResidents who live in their Spanish home also get an extra 300,000 euro allowance on that main home. We read that as not reaching a non-resident, and we would confirm it with a binding consulta before relying on it either way.\n\nThere is a second reason to file, and it catches people. A return is due where tax is payable, or where your assets and rights exceed 2,000,000 euros, counting exempt assets and without deducting debts. So a Spanish property above 2 million can mean a return with no tax to pay.\n\nThe other tax nobody mentions is the solidarity tax on large fortunes. It is still in force, prorogued indefinitely, and confirmed operative for 2026. It starts at 3,000,000 euros of net wealth, and because the 700,000 reduction applies first against a scale that charges nothing up to 3,000,000, tax in practice starts around 3.7 million. Modelo 718, filed 1 to 31 July.\n\nThe wealth tax window for assets held on 31 December opens on 8 April and closes on 30 June. File late of your own accord and it is a 1 percent surcharge plus 1 percent for every month you are late, climbing to 15 percent plus interest once you pass a year.\n\nTwo lines, two taxes, two windows. Most owners are under both and never need to think about it again.\n\nOwning or planning to buy property in Spain? Bueno is trusted by homeowners from 25+ countries. getbueno.com",
