  "title": "There is no NRA number to renew",
  "source_article": "nra-deadline.txt, rental-rule-changes.txt",
  "post_text": "The national rental registration number was struck down by the Supreme Court in May 2026. There is no state number to hold or renew.\n\nThree judgments did it, on 19 May, 21 May and 1 June 2026. The ground was competence: the State could not create that registry. So the number introduced in 2025, and the filing that went with it, are gone.\n\nThere is also no annual NRA renewal. The window of 1 February to 2 March never existed as described. What existed was an annual informative declaration during February, and the number itself was never time-limited. If you have that date in your calendar, take it out.\n\nWhat binds you is the regional licence. Regional tourist registration and licensing is unaffected by the annulments and remains fully in force. That is the file to keep current, and it is the number that has to appear on your listing.\n\nSome of the national framework survives. The Ventanilla Unica Digital and the platform data-sharing duties continue under EU Regulation 2024/1028, and platforms still have 48 hours to comply with a removal order. What fell away was the duty to check a state number, because the articles it rested on are the ones that were annulled.\n\nSo the job is simpler than it was a year ago, and it sits in one place. Your region, your municipality, your community statutes. Not Madrid.\n\nOwning or planning to buy property in Spain? Bueno is trusted by homeowners from 25+ countries. getbueno.com",
